{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGpHfQMBMzn2zE7yF3Er","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjZo5W1xbQn4X8quJgtTTN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"Y=.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; grep -n \"step_create_config\\|state_paths:\\|fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\" $Y | head -30; sed -n 120,175p $Y","description":"Find config creation and state paths"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3534,"cache_read_input_tokens":89252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3534},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:53:25.735Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GjZo5W1xbQn4X8quJgtTTN":{"command":"Y=.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; grep -n \"step_create_config\\|state_paths:\\|fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\" $Y | head -30; sed -n 120,175p $Y","description":"Find config creation and state paths"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjZo5W1xbQn4X8quJgtTTN","type":"tool_result","content":"71:  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n187:state_paths:\n230:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n233:        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n234:        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n236:        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n247:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n445:          Fan-out never reaches phase_init, so step_create_config never runs here, yet\n447:          it with step_create_config's template and populate map, the lineage_values below\n461:        populate_from: step_create_config\n702:              skip_to: step_create_config\n828:      step_create_config:\n891:          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n902:        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n920:        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n989:        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1173:        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1787:            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n2004:        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n2433:        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\n# ────────\n# SKILL REFERENCE\n# ────────\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\n# ────────\n# AGENT CONFIGURATION\n# ────────\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".skilled/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: []\n\n# ────────\n# STATE FILE PATHS\n# ────────\n# ────────\n# CANONICAL STATE WRITE MECHANISM\n# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:53:26.686Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"71:  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n187:state_paths:\n230:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n233:        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n234:        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n236:        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n247:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n445:          Fan-out never reaches phase_init, so step_create_config never runs here, yet\n447:          it with step_create_config's template and populate map, the lineage_values below\n461:        populate_from: step_create_config\n702:              skip_to: step_create_config\n828:      step_create_config:\n891:          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n902:        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n920:        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n989:        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1173:        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1787:            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n2004:        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n2433:        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\n# ────────\n# SKILL REFERENCE\n# ────────\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\n# ────────\n# AGENT CONFIGURATION\n# ────────\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".skilled/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: []\n\n# ────────\n# STATE FILE PATHS\n# ────────\n# ────────\n# CANONICAL STATE WRITE MECHANISM\n# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GjZo5W1xbQn4X8quJgtTTN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
