{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JmjJD14mJ5ZEjEQAV4qN8R","type":"tool_result","content":"## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security - Focus area: `goal_root` trust boundary (noteGoalRoot, wrapper render), completeness of the stripped git variable list (GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS, GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY/VALUE, GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES removal widening discovery), path containment of the packet inside the worktree. - Reason: rotation to D2; the trust rule for a hand-editable note field is the change's main security surface. - Rotation status: D1 done, D2-D4 remaining. - Required evidence: file:line reads of relaunch-core.cjs:496-560 and git behavior notes. Review verdict: PASS\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n * List the other checkouts of this repository that git knows as worktrees. A session can work\n * in a worktree whose packets the repository's own checkout does not hold, and git is the one\n * record of which checkouts belong to the repository. Any failure lists none.\n *\n * @param {string} repoRoot - Absolute repository root.\n * @returns {{listed: string, real: string}[]} Each worktree as git lists it and as a real\n *   path, without the repository root itself.\n */\nfunction repositoryWorktrees(repoRoot) {\n  let run;\n  try {\n    // A caller such as a git hook can export variables that point git at another repository\n    // over `-C`, and that repository's worktrees would then count as trusted here.\n    const env = { ...process.env };\n    for (const key of GIT_REPOSITORY_VARIABLES) delete env[key];\n    run = spawnSync('git', ['-C', repoRoot, 'worktree', 'list', '--porcelain'], {\n      env,\n      encoding: 'utf8',\n      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'],\n      timeout: WORKTREE_LIST_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    });\n  } catch {\n    return [];\n  }\n  if (run.error || run.status !== 0) return [];\n  const ownRoot = realPathOrNull(repoRoot);\n  const worktrees = [];\n  for (const line of String(run.stdout).split('\\n')) {\n    if (!line.startsWith('worktree ')) continue;\n    const listed = line.slice('worktree '.length);\n    const real = realPathOrNull(listed);\n    if (real === null || real === ownRoot || worktrees.some((entry) => entry.real === real)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    worktrees.push({ listed, real });\n  }\n  return worktrees;\n}\n\n// The worktree a note says its goal packet was proven in. A note is a file anyone can edit, so\n// the path counts only while git still lists it as a worktree of this repository; any other\n// directory would widen the roots a packet is checked against to anywhere on the disk.\nfunction noteGoalRoot(frontmatter, repoRoot) {\n  const goalRoot = typeof frontmatter?.goal_root === 'string' ? frontmatter.goal_root : '';\n  if (goalRoot === '' || !path.isAbsolute(goalRoot)) return '';\n  const real = realPathOrNull(goalRoot);\n  if (real === null) return '';\n  return repositoryWorktrees(repoRoot).some((entry) => entry.real === real) ? real : '';\n}\n\n/**\n * Pick the goal a note carries that its receiver may be given: the switch is on and the\n * packet still holds a goal.md, which it may have lost since the note was written. A packet\n * proven in a linked worktree comes with that worktree as its root, so the receiver reads the\n * copy the sender's goal came from.\n *","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:59:49.429Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security - Focus area: `goal_root` trust boundary (noteGoalRoot, wrapper render), completeness of the stripped git variable list (GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS, GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY/VALUE, GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES removal widening discovery), path containment of the packet inside the worktree. - Reason: rotation to D2; the trust rule for a hand-editable note field is the change's main security surface. - Rotation status: D1 done, D2-D4 remaining. - Required evidence: file:line reads of relaunch-core.cjs:496-560 and git behavior notes. Review verdict: PASS\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n * List the other checkouts of this repository that git knows as worktrees. A session can work\n * in a worktree whose packets the repository's own checkout does not hold, and git is the one\n * record of which checkouts belong to the repository. Any failure lists none.\n *\n * @param {string} repoRoot - Absolute repository root.\n * @returns {{listed: string, real: string}[]} Each worktree as git lists it and as a real\n *   path, without the repository root itself.\n */\nfunction repositoryWorktrees(repoRoot) {\n  let run;\n  try {\n    // A caller such as a git hook can export variables that point git at another repository\n    // over `-C`, and that repository's worktrees would then count as trusted here.\n    const env = { ...process.env };\n    for (const key of GIT_REPOSITORY_VARIABLES) delete env[key];\n    run = spawnSync('git', ['-C', repoRoot, 'worktree', 'list', '--porcelain'], {\n      env,\n      encoding: 'utf8',\n      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'],\n      timeout: WORKTREE_LIST_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    });\n  } catch {\n    return [];\n  }\n  if (run.error || run.status !== 0) return [];\n  const ownRoot = realPathOrNull(repoRoot);\n  const worktrees = [];\n  for (const line of String(run.stdout).split('\\n')) {\n    if (!line.startsWith('worktree ')) continue;\n    const listed = line.slice('worktree '.length);\n    const real = realPathOrNull(listed);\n    if (real === null || real === ownRoot || worktrees.some((entry) => entry.real === real)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    worktrees.push({ listed, real });\n  }\n  return worktrees;\n}\n\n// The worktree a note says its goal packet was proven in. A note is a file anyone can edit, so\n// the path counts only while git still lists it as a worktree of this repository; any other\n// directory would widen the roots a packet is checked against to anywhere on the disk.\nfunction noteGoalRoot(frontmatter, repoRoot) {\n  const goalRoot = typeof frontmatter?.goal_root === 'string' ? frontmatter.goal_root : '';\n  if (goalRoot === '' || !path.isAbsolute(goalRoot)) return '';\n  const real = realPathOrNull(goalRoot);\n  if (real === null) return '';\n  return repositoryWorktrees(repoRoot).some((entry) => entry.real === real) ? real : '';\n}\n\n/**\n * Pick the goal a note carries that its receiver may be given: the switch is on and the\n * packet still holds a goal.md, which it may have lost since the note was written. A packet\n * proven in a linked worktree comes with that worktree as its root, so the receiver reads the\n * copy the sender's goal came from.\n *","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/509-handover-worktree-goal-carry/specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/review/lineages/claude2/deep-review-strategy.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":49,"oldLines":12,"newStart":49,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->"," ## 8. WHAT WORKED","-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","+- Tracing one goal from prepare through consume, claim and both wrapper launch paths surfaced the search-order and log-tail cases (iteration 1)"," "," ---"," "," ## 9. WHAT FAILED","-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","+- Running the node suites is not possible inside the lineage write limit; test counts stay inferred (iteration 1)"," "," ---"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/509-handover-worktree-goal-carry/specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/review/lineages/claude2/deep-review-strategy.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JmjJD14mJ5ZEjEQAV4qN8R","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_typ