{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q9LXpzRpKFmFiteZp5aJkv","type":"tool_result","content":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/spec.md:33:| **Handoff Criteria** | Node suite, OpenCode plugin suite and hooks vitest all pass. The two CLI carry tests and both wrapper tests fail on the old code. The tampered-root test also passes on the old code, which ignores `goal_root` |\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/spec.md:89:- Search the linked worktrees the session log names when the usual roots hold no packet with the goal's opening line, and accept a match only when exactly one worktree and packet pair carries it.\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/spec.md:107:| `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/session-handover-cli.test.cjs` | Modify | Worktree happy path, two-worktree refusal, tampered root |\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/tasks.md:45:- [x] T003 List worktrees, search the ones the log names, and write and read `goal_root` (`C`). Verify: the three CLI worktree tests print `pass 3`.\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/tasks.md:46:- [x] T004 Write `goal_root` on prepare and report it on consume and claim (`.skilled/hooks/session-handover/bin/session-handover.cjs`). Verify: the same three tests print `pass 3`.\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/plan.md:29:The Claude goal resolver gains a last search step over the linked worktrees its session log names. A proven match writes `goal_root` beside `goal_packet`. `consume`, `claim` and the wrapper read that root back, accept it only while git lists it, and the wrapper renders the goal slice from it. Real `git worktree add` fixtures prove each step, and each new test fails on the old code.\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/implementation-summary.md:67:| `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/session-handover-cli.test.cjs` | Modified | Worktree happy path, two-worktree refusal, tampered root |\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/implementation-summary.md:93:| Fix three P2s from an independent Opus 5.5 medium review on the second Claude account | A stale `goal_root` no longer falls back to another checkout, git repository variables are stripped before listing worktrees, and the `goal_root` of the claimed note counts as named so the next hop keeps the goal. Each new test fails with its fix undone. |\n54:A missing `Goal packet:` line or `goal_packet` field is not a refusal, and `prepare` still exits 0. The goal step never fails the hand-over. It prints `[session-handover] goal not carried: <reason>` on stderr instead. `prepare` and `keep` write it only when the sender's goal can be proven. A Codex sender, a Claude session whose log cannot be read and a session whose goal has ended all leave it out. A Claude session that never had a goal set also leaves it out. That happens when neither the note's spec folder nor its parent has an unfinished `goal.md` within the slice budget. A `goal_packet` the note carried is removed on the next call in the same cases. A Claude goal whose packet exists only in a linked git worktree is carried only when the session log names that worktree's path. Otherwise the reason reads `the active goal names no packet this hand-over can find`.\n104:A session can work in a linked git worktree while its note and working directory sit in another checkout. The packet then exists only in that worktree, so the search above finds nothing. When it finds nothing, the resolver asks `git worktree list` for the repository's other checkouts. It searches only the ones the session log names a path inside, plus the `goal_root` of the note this session claimed last. Walking every worktree takes seconds, and a worktree the session never touched proves nothing about its goal. The claimed note counts because a receiver started on a worktree goal may hand over again before it touches the worktree.\n2026-11-21T22:01:28Z","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:01:29.052Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/spec.md:33:| **Handoff Criteria** | Node suite, OpenCode plugin suite and hooks vitest all pass. The two CLI carry tests and both wrapper tests fail on the old code. The tampered-root test also passes on the old code, which ignores `goal_root` |\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/spec.md:89:- Search the linked worktrees the session log names when the usual roots hold no packet with the goal's opening line, and accept a match only when exactly one worktree and packet pair carries it.\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/spec.md:107:| `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/session-handover-cli.test.cjs` | Modify | Worktree happy path, two-worktree refusal, tampered root |\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/tasks.md:45:- [x] T003 List worktrees, search the ones the log names, and write and read `goal_root` (`C`). Verify: the three CLI worktree tests print `pass 3`.\nspecs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/056-worktree-goal-carry/tasks.md:46:- [x] T004 Write `goal_root` on prepare and report it on consume and claim (`.skilled/hooks/session-handover/bin/session-handover.cjs`). Verify: the same three tests print `pass 3`.\nspec