log names that worktree's path. Otherwise the reason reads `the active goal names no packet this hand-over can find`.\n104:A session can work in a linked git worktree while its note and working directory sit in another checkout. The packet then exists only in that worktree, so the search above finds nothing. When it finds nothing, the resolver asks `git worktree list` for the repository's other checkouts. It searches only the ones the session log names a path inside, plus the `goal_root` of the note this session claimed last. Walking every worktree takes seconds, and a worktree the session never touched proves nothing about its goal. The claimed note counts because a receiver started on a worktree goal may hand over again before it touches the worktree.\n2026-11-21T22:01:28Z","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q9LXpzRpKFmFiteZp5aJkv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
