{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0134uHfU4vhta4stpXTNwuZY","type":"tool_result","content":"containment\ndeep-review-audit-ledger\ndeep-review-config.json\ndeep-review-dashboard.md\ndeep-review-effect-ledger\ndeep-review-findings-registry.json\ndeep-review-ledger\ndeep-review-state.jsonl\ndeep-review-strategy.md\ndeltas\ngraph-db\ninvocation-metadata.json\niterations\nlocks-and-fencing-v1\nreview-scope-files.txt\ntmp\n11:        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n15:             - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n16:             - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n20:          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n23:             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n25:             - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n33:             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n54:          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n60:             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n61:             - When {state_paths.findings_registry} carries a `frontier` object, list every node in `frontier.nodes` whose status is `exhausted` or `blocked` as follow-up review work: its nodeId, status, reason, scope, and `nextDimension` (or \"every dimension reviewed\" when it is null). These are the nodes a review dashboard lists as `Follow-up` lines in `## 10B. FRONTIER`; on a fan-out root, each lineage's dashboard lists its own, and the merged node ids carry the lineage label. They do not change the verdict. A registry with no `frontier` object adds nothing here.\n64:             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n66:             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n69:             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n72:             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:04:24.850Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"containment\ndeep-review-audit-ledger\ndeep-review-config.json\ndeep-review-dashboard.md\ndeep-review-effect-ledger\ndeep-review-findings-registry.json\ndeep-review-ledger\ndeep-review-state.jsonl\ndeep-review-strategy.md\ndeltas\ngraph-db\ninvocation-metadata.json\niterations\nlocks-and-fencing-v1\nreview-scope-files.txt\ntmp\n11:        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n15:             - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n16:             - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n20:          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n23:             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n25:             - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n33:             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n54:          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n60:             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n61:             - When {state_paths.findings_registry} carries a `frontier` object, list every node in `frontier.nodes` whose status is `exhausted` or `blocked` as follow-up review work: its nodeId, status, reason, scope, and `nextDimension` (or \"every dimension reviewed\" when it is null). These are the nodes a review dashboard lists as `Follow-up` lines in `## 10B. FRONTIER`; on a fan-out root, each lineage's dashboard lists its own, and the merged node ids carry the lineage label. They do not change the verdict. A registry with no `frontier` object adds nothing here.\n64:             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n66:             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n69:             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n72:             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0134uHfU4vhta4stpXTNwuZY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGq8Xn5Mqr7y2yZee5AQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015253L66zJ4uaBgjUc3cZEt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"Y=.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n 2309,2368p $Y","description":"Read report section list"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1434,"cache_read_input_tokens":199740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1434},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:04:27.596Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015253L66zJ4uaBgjUc3cZEt":{"command":"Y=.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n 2309,2368p $Y","description":"Read report section list"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015253L66zJ4uaBgjUc3cZEt","type":"tool_result","content":"          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n             - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n             - When {state_paths.findings_registry} carries a `frontier` object, list every node in `frontier.nodes` whose status is `exhausted` or `blocked` as follow-up review work: its nodeId, status, reason, scope, and `nextDimension` (or \"every dimension reviewed\" when it is null). These are the nodes a review dashboard lists as `Follow-up` lines in `## 10B. FRONTIER`; on a fan-out root, each lineage's dashboard lists its own, and the merged node ids carry the lineage label. They do not change the verdict. A registry with no `frontier` object adds nothing here.\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: a `completed-continue` extension keeps the prior review report as `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. See `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:04:28.405Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n             - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n             - When {state_paths.findings_registry} carries a `frontier` object, list every node in `frontier.nodes` whose status is `exhausted` or `blocked` as follow-up review work: its nodeId, status, reason, scope, and `nextDimension` (or \"every dimension reviewed\" when it is null). These are the nodes a review dashboard lists as `Follow-up` lines in `## 10B. FRONTIER`; on a fan-out root, each lineage's dashboard lists its own, and the merged node ids carry the lineage label. They do not change the verdict. A registry with no `frontier` object adds nothing here.\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: a `completed-continue` extension keeps the prior review report as `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. See `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015253L66zJ4uaBgjUc3cZEt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
