{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGqCqwb3mdDmmWXV2Bx9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The claude2 lineage ran all 5 iterations and the overall verdict is **PASS with advisories**: 0 P0, 0 P1, 9 P2. The run stopped on `maxIterationsReached`, as the fan-out runner requires.\n\n**Your focus question.** In the plain case, a goal set in a packet that exists only in a worktree is carried. On hop 1 the session log names the worktree. On hops 2 and 3 the claimed note's `goal_root` carries it. Every reader (`consume`, `claim` and the seeded first launch) refuses to fall back to another checkout. A few narrower cases still lose or misroute the goal:\n\n- **Log window** (`relaunch-core.cjs:910`): a worktree is only \"named\" if its path appears in the last 16 MiB of the session log. In a long session where the worktree paths are older than that, the goal is dropped.\n- **Copy in the main checkout wins** (`relaunch-core.cjs:888`): if a copy of the packet with the same title line appears in the primary checkout between hops, the next hop takes that copy over the claimed worktree. This contradicts `usableGoal`'s own rule that a worktree packet is read from that worktree or not at all.\n- **Second worktree outvotes the claimed one** (`relaunch-core.cjs:958`): if a later session's log mentions a second worktree holding the same packet, the hop refuses with \"appears in 2 packets\". It does that even though the claimed note already says which copy was proven.\n- **Stale worktree entries trusted** (security, `relaunch-core.cjs:533`): git keeps listing a deleted worktree as `prunable` until it is pruned. The code ignores that marker, so whatever later sits at that path counts as one of this repository's worktrees.\n\n**Doc and spec drift:**\n- **Tampered-root claim is wrong** (`spec.md:33`): the spec says that test passes on the old code. It now fails there, because the test plants a copy in the main checkout.\n- **Carry rule incomplete** (`troubleshooting.md:54`): it says a worktree goal is carried only when the log names the worktree. The claimed note's `goal_root` also carries it.\n- **Review fixes undocumented** (`spec.md:89`): no requirement covers the three behaviours added after the earlier second-account review. Files to Change lists 3 of the 5 new CLI tests.\n\n**Maintainability:**\n- `logTailText` duplicates the existing `readLogTail` helper.\n- One claim test builds a regex from an unescaped temp path, so a metacharacter in TMPDIR would break it.\n\nOne correction: my iteration-3 write-up wrongly said the T003 test filter matches four tests. It matches three. The correction is in iteration 4. The finding itself still stands.\n\n**Not verified:** I didn't run the test suites, because they write outside the lineage directory. So the 1073-pass count and goal.md's `validate.sh --strict` criterion are still the packet's own claims. The count does add up: 1065 plus 8 new tests.\n\nEverything this run wrote is inside the lineage directory, and the repository's changed files match the starting snapshot. A scratch `tmp/` folder inside the lineage was left in place because the workflow forbids deleting files. The report with the planning packet is `review-report.md` in the lineage directory.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:claude2"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":208997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1338},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:05:36.677Z","request_id":"<redacted>"}
